13"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T01:55:15-07:00","id":433675,"title":"","content":"i woud love a Wild west setting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21-draven","name":"Draven","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T07:07:47-07:00","id":433939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/433054-vigilant-times?p=433488#post433488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, those are the only chapters without known splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn. Thanks for the reply, though.<br /> <br /> I'll guess I'll take what I can get when it comes to Hunter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T08:14:46-07:00","id":434073,"title":"","content":"so, while Second Temple could be fun, I have already put some thought to the Book of Judges Era. Also, considering that those are two really different Eras, there is no reason why can't we work on both of them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, for Book of Judges, I've thought about a group called (temp name) Tenders of the Gods. They are a Canaanite Priesthood working to maintain the Baalim and Asheroth of the land. They see Anat is their greatest patron, although they respect all of the gods, and fight against the spawns of Yam and Mot. Another organization would be the Cult of Moloch, an antagonistic group who sacrifice the innocents to power an years old ceremony. Some bonus material could be about some rules for Empyrean beings and what is it to be a Judge.<br /> <br /> For India, the Thuggee cult could be a great opportunity to add an idea I once read (I think it was Glamourweaver who thought about it) for an organization based around the cult who hunt for the Divine Fire. They kidnap people in search for those who has that stolen fire in them and send that Fire back to Kali. May need some development, but it could be a nice concept.<br /> <br /> I have some thought about the other Eras, but I need some time to make them into something workable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T12:54:17-07:00","id":434425,"title":"","content":"Again I'd say that the difference between a Dark Era's style book and an Ancient Mysteries style book is that material in an AM style book has to be usable in a modern game. The easiest way, though obviously not the only way, is to pick time periods that are important to one of the currently active hunter groups.<br /> <br /> Any idea how to do that with the Canaanite's? Their contribution to the historical legacy is pretty minimal, and while Jewdism is the opposite, but bronze age warlords like the Judges don't create much specific legacy.<br /> <br /> The Victorian era is a good time though. Massive change, movement of hunters, monsters and ideas, it's probably when you'd start to see the first tech based Endowments (MI18). A Thuggee cult, sure, but again just cool groups isn't enough. The material should have significance and use to a modern hunter game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T13:52:09-07:00","id":434485,"title":"","content":"I think there's a basis for making the Thugee history relevant to the modern day. I mean, whether the historical group existed or not in the real world, the fall out was that the British Empire ultimately enforced multiple Criminal Tribes Acts which branded certain ethnic groups as genetically predisposed to criminality. Ultimately leading to these groups being forced into what amount to concentration camps, and even after independance they're still extremely maginalised groups.<br /> <br /> There could still be a small ember of an older hunter conspiracy, kinda a reverse Loyalists; keeping up the vigil despite wider society perhaps not deserving it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T14:04:44-07:00","id":434500,"title":"","content":"I think that's the right kind of thinking for a Ancient Mysteries style Hunter book <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Though that specific example comes across as a bit self indulgent IMO. &quot;We're heroes and society are all arseholes&quot;. I feel you can do one or the other before it gets a bit much).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T14:33:28-07:00","id":434563,"title":"","content":"I was thinking more like the Forsaken from Werewolf. They have a duty they only imperfectly remember, but they keep to it because it's all they have left of their former identity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T14:37:14-07:00","id":434568,"title":"","content":"Ka-ching!<br /> <br /> I'd still suggest a broader British Empire period though; that way some of the cannon groups can be tied in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T01:55:22-07:00","id":435476,"title":"","content":"Here are the eras I've been tinkering with the most<br /> <br /> - Book of Judges Era, as inspired by the Kickstarter era we didn't get; this is a MtC-crossover Era in my head<br /> - Vigil for Rome - contemporary with Requiem for Rome, but doesn't go with the Paterfamillias version of the Aves Minerva because they just come off as too generically Roman to me, and I much prefer diverse groups that represent different cultural phenomena. I've got 3 primary Compacts, and 3 Conspiracies for that one (with 2 other groups of each type getting sidebar coverage as they're fully playable by reskinning other groups or using the modern versions of themselves).<br /> - Birth of the Haudenosaunee (Iroquois League) - introduces Sons of Sosondowah Conspiracy called to action to uphold the Great Law by Hiawatha and Deganawida themselves<br /> - I'd LIKE to do an 1830s India setting that combines Hunter with an expansion on the periods Vampires (see Ancient Mysteries/Ancient Bloodlines), but I don't have strong enough concepts yet for Indian Hunter groups, other than the one major Conspiracy I created, the Prarabdhavat, a small (like Lucifuge scale) group of Hindu and Theravada Buddhist Hunters aware of their past lives who bring karmic retribution to those immortals who otherwise evade karma by their nature. But they should be far from the only ones.<br /> - WW2","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T08:16:45-07:00","id":435715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/433054-vigilant-times?p=434425#post434425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again I'd say that the difference between a Dark Era's style book and an Ancient Mysteries style book is that material in an AM style book has to be usable in a modern game. The easiest way, though obviously not the only way, is to pick time periods that are important to one of the currently active hunter groups.<br /> <br /> Any idea how to do that with the Canaanite's? Their contribution to the historical legacy is pretty minimal, and while Jewdism is the opposite, but bronze age warlords like the Judges don't create much specific legacy..</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, I have thought about that. A lesser known fact is that during the early days of modern Israel there was a movement named the Council for the Coalition of the Hebrew Youth, or as they were more commonly known, the Canaanite. They were a radical left wing movement who claimed that Israel shouldn't encourage, or even allow, new Jews to come to Israel and should instead focus about the connection between the &quot;Hebrews&quot;, as well as the other people in the region, and their land. Considering that this is the World of Darkness, maybe a splinter group of that movement has searched after more.. direct ways to strength that connection, and rediscovered the old practices of the old Priesthood, and by adopting those rites in a new tradition they work to unite the people and the land together. They could work either as a conspiracy of a compact, IMO.<br /> <br /> The Cult of Moloch, however, never truly died out. Gei Ben Hinom may have been purified and Carthage may have fallen, but the rite stil exist, and the cult is still around- and maybe even spread outside of the Mediterranean. This is still an Horror game, after all- and there is nothing more scary then an ancient conspiracy dedicated for killing.<br /> <br /> About a &quot;Judge&quot; mechanics, adapting them for a modern setting could be easy. People are still chosen by higher ideas to fulfill a certain mission. What chose them is unknown- call it God, or the Empyrean, or Sophia or maybe it is even just a.. principle. Something motivates that person toward a certain Agenda, and that thing manifest itself at a certain ability with which that person is &quot;blessed&quot;. I think that they should be called something like the Inspired, and have a two-tier system like Slashers based around a certain advantage.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T12:48:22-07:00","id":436062,"title":"","content":"<u><b>Countercultural United States</b></u><br /> <br /> The countercultural revolution was a turbulent time for the vigil. A young generation eager to escape the stifling culture of their parents unearthed monsters and occult law as they explored new scientific, philosophical and spiritual ideas. To historians of the Vigil, such that they are, the countercultural revolution is often seen as a continuation or final resurgence of The War. Once again powerful Conspiracies were shaken and new groups formed to fill the vacuum.<br /> <br /> If the stormy sixties were a continuation of The War than they were a continuation in more than spirit. The Shadow of World War II still loomed large over the Vigil, without the destructions of many established Conspiracies during the War (and European Colonisation centuries before) the events of the decade simply could not have taken place. Ideas and discoveries that gave birth to Cells and Compacts in the 1960s would have been prevented or appropriated a few decades earlier by Conspiracies eager to protect their monopoly or destroy whatever foul monster a well meaning student might blunder into.<br /> <br /> Other historians say that the counter cultural revolution was not a continuation. It was the pendulum swinging back towards the centre as a young generation explored new philosophical and spiritual ideas; bringing a sense of mysticism and a spirit of revolution to counterbalance the predominately technological and government backed organisations born in the fires of The War. Many of the groups were overtly political, with strong ties to civilian politics.<br /> <br /> Whether it was an echo or the returning pendulum; the stormy sixties were but a puff of air before the howling fury of The War, the alliances forged were mere Compacts compared to the grand Conspiracies backed by the might of Empires that arose in previous decades. Indeed, by the decade's end most of them had been consumed by larger groups eager to plunder their knowledge, censor unAmerican activities, or assert their monopolies on certain areas of occult lore.<br /> <hr /><br /> So after this opening I'm thinking fiction pieces, pieces of lore for existing orgs, and maybe new orgs who might or might not survive onto the present day. Basically, keep the openings small.<br /> <br /> I chose to start with a really recent piece because IMO working backwards will help. From this alone it's clear that in WWII and Native American hunter we should be mentioning some Conspiracies that were destroyed or damaged during WWII and thus led to the countercultural compacts.<br /> <br /> I've also got some brainstorms for things I can include; but I don't want to go overboard. Short focused periods IMO:<br /> <br /> Groups founded during the era - Maiden's Blood Sisterhood, Illuminated Brotherhood.<br /> <br /> A civil rights group where almost everyone has mixed membership with The Union or The Long Night. It's eventual fate is to slowly dissolve back into the previous two groups when the Civil Rights movement slows down.<br /> <br /> A Null Mysteriis cell dedicated to reverse engineering WWII supertech (Nazi or MI18 mostly) for the good of mankind. Eventual fate: Conscripted by TF:V, but not before they destroyed their research.<br /> <br /> A not-psychic-but-want-to-be group drawing on LSD, Uri Geller, and similar. Some temporay successes but nothing lasting or repeatable. Fate: A few prison sentences for drugs. Cherion hears of it and grabs the competent members for research; offers Field Projects Devision jobs to the rest but gets few takers and doesn't see any need to insist. Cherion overlooks Barbra Wintergreen who's a mere undergrand and in jail.<br /> <br /> TF:V: Shifting from a war footing to a peacekeeping footing. ADAMANSKI grows in promimence over TWILIGHT, rooting out monsters, commies, and KSI21 in american politics; naturally a lot of false positives and general McCarthism. McCarthy paranoia reaches it's peak when ADAMANSKI discovers that witches are jumping onto the countercultural revolution (the rise of the Free Council, though it's left open so STs can replace Awakened with Hunter style Witches if they prefer) and supports Vampires in response. This is a direct parallel to funding the Taliban against the Soviet Union and will have it's own 9/11 style consiquences - but without a cannon 9/11 like event that might have to be left as an implication.<br /> <br /> TF:V, KSI 21, MI18; Cold War!<br /> <br /> Null Mysteriis: I'm thinking the origin of TF:V's etheric bullets through pocket protecting pencil pushing nuclear physics geeks aiming to better humanity but get conscripted instead. etheric bullets can't be much later than KSI 21 projection.<br /> <br /> Ashwood Abbey - maybe a really short section on straight laced by day, Abbey by night.<br /> <br /> Keepers of the Source; busy manipulating lay lines to create resonances of peace and love - but edging into turf war for lay line control with Witches. (Which is why I shouldn't write anything for the Keepers)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 03-10-2015, 04:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T15:28:23-07:00","id":436342,"title":"","content":"sounds interesting- I do wonder what organizations are there for France and the Axis Powers (sure, playing a fascist, if not a Nazi, does seems a bit too much for most people- but I do assume those Powers should have some sort of hunter orgs)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-10T15:36:12-07:00","id":436352,"title":"","content":"That's WWII not 1960s <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Check my sig for occupied France's compact - Society de Hadies. Basically the french resistance using the Underworld to hide and travel unseen; there be lots of helpful French ghosts during that time period.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T02:44:21-07:00","id":438219,"title":"","content":"McCarthyism wasn't really aimed at any counter-culture; it was aimed at actual communists/former communists with actual links to the former Comintern. Also, it's a good 10 years before the counter-culture really takes off. I think the link to the Free Council is a really great idea mind you.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't stop the era at just the 60s. The counter-culture is more a late 60s into the 70s phenomena. I mean, a big focus politically is opposition to the Vietnam war which drags on to the mid-70s, but only really escalates in the mid-60s. What's noticable (and relevant for Hunter I think), is that there's an increasing militant vibe to it with the influence of urban guerilla groups in Europe, but that only really gets going in the 70s.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T04:31:12-07:00","id":438271,"title":"","content":"Off hand idea for the signatory orgs of the Candellight Compact in Revolutionary-era Philadelphia. Note that many of the Tier 2 Groups are larger than the Tier 3 ones in the colonies, the Tier 3 ones just have more reach elsewhere in the world.<br /> <br /> Tier 3<br /> - Acheron Shipping and Trading Guild<br /> - Lucifuge<br /> - Malleus Maleficarum<br /> - Novus Ordo Seclorum (Masonic-offspring of the Knights of St George, and the Enlightenment researchers of the &quot;Lightbringers&quot; of the last century; dedicated to freeing human enlightenment and self-rule from the supernatural; some historic links to VALKYRIE, though the latter would be unrecognizable to the former)<br /> <br /> Tier 2<br /> - Midnightmen (play on &quot;Minutemen&quot; - the era's version of the Union)<br /> - [Puritan group that is reminiscent of the militant wing of Long Night]<br /> - [Quaker schism from the above, that is reminiscent of the merciful wing of the Long Night]<br /> - Les Voyaguers (with the French-Indian war in resent memories, they're even less trusted than the Lucifuge by the others)<br /> - [Privateer company that protects business interests from the supernatural for profit, associated closely with a certain Caribbean-born nouve-riche bastard New Yorker....]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T11:37:01-07:00","id":438730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/433054-vigilant-times?p=438219#post438219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">McCarthyism wasn't really aimed at any counter-culture; it was aimed at actual communists/former communists with actual links to the former Comintern. Also, it's a good 10 years before the counter-culture really takes off. I think the link to the Free Council is a really great idea mind you.</div> </div> </div> </div> That works too,<br /> <br /> TF:V started playing America to the Kindred's Asfganistan a decade earlier. That gives plenty of time for the TF:V - Vampire connection to become firmly entrenched as The Man that counter cultural Compacts &amp; the Canites protest too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/433054-vigilant-times?p=438219#post438219\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't stop the era at just the 60s.</div> </div> </div> </div> I don't intend to. I shouldn't use the phrase &quot;the 60s.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/433054-vigilant-times?p=438271#post438271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Off hand idea for the signatory orgs of the Candellight Compact in Revolutionary-era Philadelphia.</div> </div> </div> </div> I have to admit the Candlelight Compact is one of the least interesting hunter eras to me; I prefer focusing on one group at a time.<br /> <br /> That said, it is a big part of the setting so I won't object to it going in. I just probably won't be writing for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T19:50:10-07:00","id":439253,"title":"","content":"The Sons of Sosondowah might also be signatories to the Candlelight Compact - but I might have them be present, agree to the principles, but refuse to sign - on the grounds that there is a clear &quot;American Independence&quot; alignment to the pact, and the Confederation is trying to maintain neutrality as best it can (the war ends up being the only time in history different nations of the Haudenosaunee fought against each other in war).<br /> <br /> If anyone's curious as to what brings down Novus Ordo Seclorum, a combination of three factors - <br /> <br /> 1) External anti-Masonic public pressure in the early 19th Century<br /> <br /> 2) Infighting as a good half the members believe that they're fighting for the liberation of ALL human beings; while another third believe that among those human rights they're fighting for is to own humans as property.<br /> <br /> 3) Mystic infiltration. Like HYDRA inside SHIELD [if you haven't seen Winter Soldier yet, it's your own damn fault], supernatural agents exist inside NOS like a gestalting seed. Whether it's the Seers of the Throne, a Tef-Aabhi Cult (either fit the Pyramid symbology), or someone else I intend to leave vague for the individual table - but there is supernatural subversion from within that will come to ahead with these other factors by the 1820s and 30s.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyone of these the Conspiracy could have survived, but together they shattered it into individually operating Chapter-houses, that weren't really even networked enough to qualify as Tier 2.<br /> <br /> By 1865 though, the founders of the Shadow Service within the Secret Service include a couple of elderly former NOS Masonic hunters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T23:22:32-07:00","id":440935,"title":"","content":"So I have the Roman-era Collegium Aesculapii as the public face of the much older Kheironos Mysterio. Is my Latin and Ancient Greek (respectively) correct as far as you can tell?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-14-2015, 02:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T11:08:43-07:00","id":442828,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/433054-vigilant-times?p=436352#post436352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's WWII not 1960s <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Check my sig for occupied France's compact - Society de Hadies. Basically the french resistance using the Underworld to hide and travel unseen; there be lots of helpful French ghosts during that time period.</div> </div> </div> </div>didn't really got the reference, but I know of the Society and I like them. I wonder if I could work a version of my Aki Ten for Japan in the WWII (I think that Onmyodo has already lost its political power during that time, so maybe they are compact during that time. I'll use any excuse to make myself giving them a better treatment :P)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-19T21:11:36-07:00","id":450100,"title":"","content":"Just an offhand thought about the Medieval Period...<br /> <br /> Tier 2<br /> - Bogatyrs: Slavic brotherhood of adventurers, concerned with glory and protecting the vulnerable... at least in theory<br /> <br /> - Bon Hommes: despite their name, the &quot;Good Men&quot; are actually the most gender egalitarian Hunter Compact of the era, these Cathar ascetics seek to subvert the machinations (hehehe... get it... machinations) of the Demiurge that keeps mankind trapped in its material cycle (*cough*gears*cough*)<br /> <br /> - Ma'asei Merkavah: this Jewish Compact will one day be a full fledged Conspiracy, but in this era their scholarly pursuit of holy truth and Divine Names has yet to bear their future Endowments; think of them as a very differently culturally flavored version of the Loyalists of Thule (without the whole debt to others thing, they're laser focused on holy mysteries and their own community)<br /> <br /> - Salat al-Layl: More than any other Compact, the &quot;Night's Prayer&quot; fills the &quot;community defenders&quot; niche with their dedication to the Umma<br /> <br /> - Twilight Company: A free company that specializes in combating the unnatural for the highest bidder... including for bidders that may themselves be other than natural<br /> <br /> <br /> Tier 3<br /> - Aegis Kai Doru: based in the &quot;Byzantine&quot; (Eastern Roman) Empire, and spanning through the rest of Eastern Christendom via the Orthodox and Coptic Churches<br /> <br /> - Ascending Ones: spread through the Muslim world (though with a diverse members base) from Al-Andalus to the Ghurid Sultanate<br /> <br /> - Lucifuge: hidden through some of the oldest families in Europe, and the occasional peasant bastard<br /> <br /> - Red Crusade: based in Western Christendom , this predecessor of Malleus Maleficarum lacks its obsession with vampires, concerning itself first and foremost with things demonic, and sorcery in the hands of the enemies of the Church. The increasingly heretical Knights of Saint George are a faction of this Conspiracy that have yet to schism.<br /> <br /> <br /> [[as someone is likely to ask - my thinking on Cheiron's history is that it has been destroyed and reformed multiple times when the Sign is rediscovered and a cult forms around it, often involving digging up lost research of past incarnations - this era is one of the gaps in its history, before the Acheron Shipping and Trading Guild will be born in the 15th Century]]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-20-2015, 12:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T06:34:53-07:00","id":450382,"title":"","content":"Entirely biased but I love the idea of &quot;Wars of Scottish Independence&quot; Hunter. Might mockup an elevator pitch later","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T14:18:45-07:00","id":450892,"title":"","content":"Are we going to do any work for this, or just brainstorm forever <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> BTW Glamourweaver, I'd strongly suggest you pick a location rather than just &quot;medieval times&quot;. If either Hakollel or Ma'asei is going into this... well we'll have to discuss that at some point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T15:13:49-07:00","id":450925,"title":"","content":"I think that the best way to work on this project would be that each person would say what is he or she is planing to work on, and how those things would be connected with each other. Personally, I'm going to write the reincarnation of the Canaanite priesthood (I think about making them into a movement which seeks to bring stability to the Middle East by renewing the old contracts with the gods and constructing ancient idols- maybe with adding some Mummy antagonistic connection for fun), the Cult of Moloch (as something in the form of the Promethean Brotherhood and the Hunt Club- only bigger), the Chosen/Inspired &quot;evolved template&quot; (working like Slashers and inspired by the Old Hunter) and adapting the Aki Ten into the group they were in the WWII (I think it could be interesting- from one side, they are considered to be the enemies of the Allies. On the other, they aren't all that satisfied with the current situation, and may see the war as an opportunity to reclaim their past influence)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkydel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/433054-vigilant-times?p=450382#post450382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Entirely biased but I love the idea of &quot;Wars of Scottish Independence&quot; Hunter. Might mockup an elevator pitch later</div> </div> </div> </div>could you please sell me on that? It is just that it sounds interesting, but I don't really know much about that event and the atmosphere which should be around it.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-20T16:53:54-07:00","id":450999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/433054-vigilant-times?p=450892#post450892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are we going to do any work for this, or just brainstorm forever <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> BTW Glamourweaver, I'd strongly suggest you pick a location rather than just &quot;medieval times&quot;. If either Hakollel or Ma'asei is going into this... well we'll have to discuss that at some point.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know - it was just an offhand though about if the NWoD addressed the same scale setting that CWoD Dark Ages setting does, to provide some context for a more specific subject. I agree any Dark Eras type chapter would have a MUCH narrower focus.<br /> <br /> If I was going to do something off the period, I'd either do focus on Cathars vs. the God Machine in Western Europe leading up the Albigensian Crusade; or do the Levant in the Third Crusade, with a specific focus on the Knights of St George on the Crusaders side, and the Ascending Ones' uncomfortable relationship with Saladin's forces.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T06:36:37-07:00","id":452614,"title":"","content":"Actually the more I think about it, the more I like the Albigensian Cathars period in Western Europe as a Hunter/Demon crossover Era, that would include Bon Hommes (Cathars) as its signature Compact, and the Red Crusade (Roman Church) as its signature Conspiracy - with the Lucifuge in a background player role.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 03-22-2015, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T07:27:36-07:00","id":452637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/433054-vigilant-times?p=450925#post450925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">could you please sell me on that? It is just that it sounds interesting, but I don't really know much about that event and the atmosphere which should be around it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, for me (as a Scotsman), on the one hand it's one of those areas of history that very rarely gets attention- and when it does it tends to be handled rather badly. We're talking about events that have this profound sense of upheaval, a feeling that hasn't entirely evaporated even by the present day.<br /> <br /> There's the rich and varied tapestry of the Scottish landscape, a place where numerous evils could hide. The hills and glens, the caves and the deeps of Lochs. The perpetual shadows of a land so wild, and a people so spirited, that even Rome couldn't tame her. Perhaps the Compacts rose from humble beginnings, the spirited warriors who kept home and hearth safe in the long watches of the night. But such things are conventional evils, no true match for the ambitions of men and the politics of beasts.<br /> <br /> Do Vampires control the fate of nations? Do they pit England and Scotland against one another for petty gains? Wolves run the land amidst the tumult of war, battlefields draw those who seek the unquiet dead. These things and stranger horrors surface, in the chaos of conflict.<br /> Did the Stone of Destiny hold any true power? Why was it a Spider that inspired Robert the Bruce?<br /> <br /> I like the idea of having the Guardians of Scotland as a low-powered conspiracy or as a high-powered local Compact; looking to protect Scotland from threats both external and internal, both mundane and supernatural. Potentially from dark powers that have dwelt in the land since ages long gone past. Maybe a nod or two to the oWoD, given its penchant for having unfathomable gribblyness in ye olde Caledonia <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;The phrase 'flies on the heads of pins' appeared 43 times in that journal, sometimes in the middle of sentences or written in the margins.&quot;","edited":{"userid":4871,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","user":"Malkydel","date":". 03-22-2015, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4871-malkydel","name":"Malkydel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4871_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T15:22:01-07:00","id":453250,"title":"","content":"<b>The Man is Sucking Me Dry</b><br /> <br /> For almost as long as the student protesters imagined some white guy in a suit as The Man counter-cultural Hunters of all stripes and backgrounds were picturing The Man as a very white guy in an opera cape. To understand how Vampires became the prime evil for a generation of Hunters you must go back in time.<br /> <br /> Two decades ago Task Force: VALKARIE had a problem, that problem was communism, and also Witches. The Task Force's increasing competence at getting information out Witch society had unearthed a recent and growing vein of socialism in witch society. To say the Men in Black were terrified would be putting it mildly, but between their regular monster hunting duties and Ivan VALAKRIE just didn't have the resources to open a third front, and so they made a Faustian bargain that still haunts them them to this day. They funded vampires to fight a proxy war against the witches.<br /> <br /> But to get the full story you must go back even earlier, to America's shameful history of slavery. Vampires are timeless creatures, and rather predictable in their way. They need blood, and slaves were an almost limitless supply. In turn the Cainite Heresy, who only see race as \u201chuman, vampire and everyone else\u201d, did as they always had done and recruited the vampire's victims, slaves and abolitionists alike.<br /> <br /> In the 1960s these two stories combined in a perfect storm that would define a generation of the American Vigil.<br /> <br /> By the time the counter-cultural came around centuries of predation had created an enormous concentration of Canites among African Americans; a young, angry, heavily armed, black man in the 60s could be explain himself in one of two ways: Civil rights activist or vampire hunter. Unsurprisingly the Canites chose the former and quickly became vocal and well placed members of the civil rights movement; despite their unworkable vampire-centric theory of race relations.<br /> <br /> The Canites, or Hunters in general, embedding themselves in revolutionary movements is nothing new. The experienced Vampire knows when to fade away and let mortals figure it out, and that's just what would have happened if the experienced vampires hadn't been usurped two decades earlier by younger monsters with equipment, funding, and most importantly, cover ups courtesy of Uncle Sam. What's more, many of the new Vampire elite were slave owners in life and took the civil rights movement rather personally.<br /> <br /> And so the Canites dragged counter-culture hunters into their conflict with vampires, the vampires brought in the Men in Black, and for a generation of hunters the Man had Fangs.<br /> <br /> [Picture: A canite hunter, base him on old photos of the Black Panthers, stands on top of a stone staircase, the kind you'll see outside government buildings or the Lincoln Memorial. He rests one foot on a staked vampire and has a circle on his head (see the Canite in NS p153). He's currently in a Mexican stand-off against two police officers, holding one pistol in each hand, the Canite symbol floats behind each gun.]<br /> <hr /><br /> So that's a first draft. I like it quite a lot, but I couldn't find a way to fit in how the vampire and TF:V relationship actually works which I feel is kinda important. Basically, the vampire's know that TF:V could kill them. TF:V knows that the vampires can leak all the USA's secrets. Mutually assured destruction.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}